From 5c06fb8b82edc8b54bf545d0c2a9f23755ec6b4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher AMIAUD <christopher.amiaud@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:36:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Implement pipes in-process for threaded fork()

Emscripten's pipes don't report end of file reliably once processes
are threads sharing the host's fds, so the reader of a pipeline could
wait forever. Under HAVE_THREADED_FORK, a pipe is now a ring buffer
in blink that counts the fds open on either end. Writes block while
it's full, and fail with EPIPE once no reader is left.

sendfile() now goes through the fd callbacks, as read() and write()
do, so it works with these pipes too. It also resumes a partial write
where it stopped, instead of writing the start of the buffer again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
